  "robot_info_version": "0.2",

  "name": "Omnemo OS",
  "tagline": "Omarchy, made easy, made for memory: a friendlier desktop layer for Omarchy with Omnemo shared AI memory built in.",
  "summary": "Omnemo OS is an edition of the Omarchy Linux desktop, installed as a layer on top of a stock Omarchy 4.5 computer, not a fork. One command adds a bar along the bottom with a taskbar, plain-words menus (Tools, Favorites, a wrench for settings), a \"?\" guide to every icon and a flag-style bar look; switches workspaces to floating windows; and installs Omnemo so the AI helpers already on the computer share one memory. It backs up everything it touches first, and `omnemo-os uninstall` puts the computer back byte for byte, keeping the memories unless the person types DELETE.",
  "version": "0.9.3",
  "status": "Public Preview. 1.0 waits for one test: a full Omarchy version update on a stock computer with the edition on.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "homepage": "https://projectsparks.ai/omnemo-os",
  "source": "https://github.com/GuyMannDude/omnemo-os",
  "contact": "https://github.com/GuyMannDude/omnemo-os/issues",
  "maintainer": "Project Sparks",
  "not_affiliated": "Built on Omarchy (MIT). Not affiliated with or endorsed by Omarchy's owners.",

  "capabilities": [
    "A layer, not a fork: everything is user-level (no sudo), written only under the person's home folder.",
    "Version gate: installs only on Omarchy 4.5 stable or newer (package omarchy >= 4.5.0-1); a 4.5.0 pre-release only with --allow-rc; anything older is refused before any change.",
    "Refuses before changing anything if a file it would create is already there and not its own, or if it is already installed.",
    "Backs up first: shell.json, the workspace-layouts folder, hyprland.lua, bindings.lua, looknfeel.lua, the Omarchy menu file and every other managed file go to ~/.local/state/omnemo-os/backup/<UTC time>/, and the install record ~/.local/state/omnemo-os/installed.json is written BEFORE any change, so even an install that dies partway can be undone.",
    "Seven bar plugins: guy.taskbar (AI, Browsers, Web apps, Files, Apps, Settings, one icon per open window), guy.tools (Tools menu), guy.help (\"?\" guide with live memory numbers), guy.favorites, guy.utils (wrench: Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, Display, Sound, Weather, clocks, calendar, all settings), guy.clock, guy.flag (the flag-style bar).",
    "Desktop settings it changes: bar at the bottom, solid background under the flag layer, its own bar layout, stock dock off, floating workspaces by default, new floating windows centred and sized to fit above the bar, an Apps entry in the Omarchy menu, Super+Alt+Space opens the Apps list, Super+M minimizes to the taskbar on every kind of workspace, no pointer jump on a taskbar switch.",
    "Everyday extras: a one-bar guard (systemd user timer, every 30 s, keeps exactly one bar running), friendly names (foot → Terminal, Calculator, Writer), text files open in Writer, stand-ins for two missing icon sets, a Hwy 180 wallpaper choice (never set as the current wallpaper).",
    "Colored bar icons: downloads the Papirus icon set (GPL-3.0, release 20260801, checksum checked) into its own folder; offline, the bar uses one-color glyphs and `omnemo-os repair` fetches them later.",
    "Memory: if Omnemo is not installed, installs it the Omnemo INSTALL.md way at a pinned, reviewed commit (venv, pip from GitHub, link, `omnemo setup`), registering it only with AI helpers that are really installed (it never downloads Claude Code, Codex or others). If Omnemo is already installed it is left exactly as it is.",
    "Uninstall restores every managed file byte for byte (content and file mode) from the install-day backup, even after any number of updates; it removes the Omnemo it installed (never one that was there before) and asks before touching the memories.",
    "Status, repair and update: `status` shows what is installed and flags what an Omarchy update reset; `repair` puts it back and connects newly installed AI helpers; `update` moves to the newest release tag without questions."
  ],

  "exposes": {
    "cli": [
      {"command": "bin/omnemo-os install [--allow-rc]", "purpose": "Install the edition (run from the cloned folder). --allow-rc accepts an Omarchy 4.5.0 pre-release."},
      {"command": "omnemo-os status", "purpose": "What is installed (memory and icons included), which AI helpers have the memory, and anything an Omarchy update reset. Prints the 'BEFORE your next Omarchy update' line when it applies."},
      {"command": "omnemo-os repair", "purpose": "Put back what an Omarchy update reset (friendly names, the guard, the command link, icons, a failed memory install) and connect AI helpers installed since. Safe to run any time."},
      {"command": "omnemo-os update [--allow-rc]", "purpose": "From the installed command: fetch the newest release tag and hand over to it. From a downloaded copy (`./bin/omnemo-os update`): apply that copy. Asks nothing; never goes backwards; keeps memories and the person's own changes."},
      {"command": "omnemo-os uninstall", "purpose": "Restore the computer to how it was before the first install. Asks \"Keep your memories? [Y/n]\" when it removes an Omnemo it installed."},
      {"command": "omnemo-icons-update [--pin TAG SHA]", "purpose": "Fetch the newest colored icon set (or a pinned release with its checksum)."},
      {"command": "omarchy snapshot create", "purpose": "Omarchy's own snapshot (asks for the password). The README's step 1 before installing."}
    ],
    "keyboard": [
      {"keys": "Super + L", "purpose": "Change how windows sit on the current workspace. The bar's ? guide says it steps through floating, side by side and a sliding row."},
      {"keys": "Super + M", "purpose": "Minimize the window to the taskbar (any workspace layout)."},
      {"keys": "Super + Alt + Space", "purpose": "Open the Apps list."}
    ]
  },

  "configuration": {
    "file": "~/.config/omarchy/shell.toml — the install appends a marked block with a [flag] table. Edit values there; the commented lines list the choices.",
    "flag_keys": [
      {"key": "flag.motion", "default": "auto", "values": "auto | full | calm | off", "changes": "auto = ripple on mains power, still on battery and on a computer that draws without a graphics card (most virtual machines). full = always ripple. calm = slower, gentler. off = a still flag."},
      {"key": "flag.blue", "default": "\"#435ECE\" (set by the install; the plugin's own default is #3C3B6E)", "changes": "Colour of the fields behind each icon group."},
      {"key": "flag.red", "default": "#C21F35", "changes": "Stripe colour."},
      {"key": "flag.white", "default": "#FFFFFF", "changes": "Stripe colour."},
      {"key": "flag.stripes", "default": 5, "values": "3 to 7", "changes": "Number of stripes."},
      {"key": "flag.stars", "default": "on", "values": "0 turns them off", "changes": "A star at the end of each blue field that has room."},
      {"key": "flag.depth", "default": "on", "values": "0 turns it off", "changes": "0 = the flat 0.9.2 flag: no shine, no motion."}
    ],
    "environment": [
      {"name": "XDG_CONFIG_HOME", "default": "~/.config", "changes": "Where the Omarchy, Hyprland and systemd user files it manages are found."},
      {"name": "XDG_STATE_HOME", "default": "~/.local/state", "changes": "Where the install record and backups go (<XDG_STATE_HOME>/omnemo-os/)."},
      {"name": "XDG_DATA_HOME", "default": "~/.local/share", "changes": "Where the installed copy, icons, Omnemo venv and memory store live."},
      {"name": "MISE_DATA_DIR", "default": "<XDG_DATA_HOME>/mise", "changes": "Where it looks for really-installed AI helpers."},
      {"name": "OMNEMO_OS_URL", "default": "https://github.com/GuyMannDude/omnemo-os", "changes": "Where `omnemo-os update` looks for release tags."}
    ],
    "layout": "The bar layout it writes is layout.json in the repo (bar.layout in ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json). A layout you change after install is yours: update leaves it alone and says so.",
    "colors_menus": "Every menu, label and icon choice lives in the QML files under plugins/. They are replaced by `omnemo-os update`; a plugin you edited is saved to ~/.local/state/omnemo-os/replaced/<time>/plugins/ first."
  },

